ur fix your heart tv  you interview people about being kind  um and david you know  is it would it be okay if you quickly  interviewed uh lonnie and i  both right now for fix your heart tv  would you be up for that yes  absolutely i've got some prepared  questions okay perfect  when you realize you've hurt someone by  your actions  how do you fix your heart well you know  the whole purpose  and the whole definition of fix your  heart is to have the accountability to  correct your own actions and be better  to others and mainly sometimes just  yourself and  i mean how do i fix my own heart have  the accountability to say sorry  100 i uh  i feel like that is probably where i  hold myself the most accountable  i wish i had half a quarter  one percent of the concern for myself  that i do for others  which is probably a good start and maybe  enough sometimes but if i ever do things  that i  think don't feel right  i i really hold myself accountable  lonnie would you like to extend the same  questions to david if you don't mind  oh a hundred percent let's go  well um now you have both  been in the business before the time of  social media unlike me  and social media has given canceling  people a  whole culture making mistakes are  inevitable though because we are human  of course so miss drew do you worry  about making a mistake  and being canceled  yeah um i never want to  say things or do things that hurts  anybody  um because it's the last thing on earth  i want to do  i don't want to affect other people  negatively david what do you think  gosh it's a really great question um  i mean first and foremost you know i do  try to live by  treat each other's as you would like to  be treated  um and so you know to have compassion to  have kindness  to have empathy um  is the way to lead to understand you  know and and  for me personally as a black person  especially  you know i know what  it feels like to be willfully  misunderstood mistreated  uh marginalized and so i absolu